/*
Problem: Minimum Element After Replacement With Digit Sum (LC 3300)
Topic: Array / Math

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Replace every number by the sum of
its digits.

Among all the digit sums, return the
minimum one.

Instead of modifying the entire array,
compute the digit sum for each number
and keep track of the smallest value.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Initialize:

   minNumber = INT_MAX

2. Traverse every number.

3. Compute its digit sum by repeatedly:

   • Extract last digit.

   • Add it to the sum.

   • Remove the last digit.

4. Update the minimum digit sum.

5. Return the minimum.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[10,12,13,14]

Digit sums:

10 → 1

12 → 3

13 → 4

14 → 5

Minimum:

1

Answer:

1

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[999,25,101]

Digit sums:

999 → 27

25 → 7

101 → 2

Minimum:

2

Answer:

2

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Each number is processed independently.

Its digit sum is calculated using
modulo (%) and division (/).

The smallest digit sum encountered is
the required answer.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n × d)

n = number of elements

d = maximum digits in a number

Since d ≤ 10 for integers,
this is effectively O(n).

Space : O(1)

Only a few variables are used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Array Traversal / Digit Manipulation
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int minElement(vector<int>& nums) {

        int minNumber = INT_MAX;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            int sum = 0;

            // Compute digit sum
            while (nums[i] > 0) {

                sum += nums[i] % 10;
                nums[i] /= 10;
            }

            minNumber = min(minNumber, sum);
        }

        return minNumber;
    }
};
